  "Question": "If you walk for \\(45\\) minutes at a rate of \\(4\\) mph and then run for \\(30\\) minutes at a rate of \\(10\\) mph, how many miles have you gone at the end of one hour and \\(15\\) minutes?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3.5\\) miles",
    "B": "\\(8\\) miles",
    "C": "\\(9\\) miles",
    "D": "\\(25\\dfrac13\\) miles",
    "E": "\\(480\\) miles"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Because the speeds are in miles per hour, first express the times in hours. The walking time is \\(45/60=3/4\\) hour, and the running time is \\(30/60=1/2\\) hour. Distance equals speed times time, so the two distances are\n\\[\n4\\cdot\\frac34=3\\text{ miles},\\qquad 10\\cdot\\frac12=5\\text{ miles}.\n\\]\nThese two stages fill the entire \\(75\\) minutes. The total distance is \\(3+5=8\\) miles, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
